---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Label from "../components/Label.astro";
import { breadcrumbSchema } from "../schema";
import { ORG, CONTACT, LEGAL_EFFECTIVE_DATE } from "../consts";

const schemas = [
  breadcrumbSchema([
    { name: "Home", path: "/" },
    { name: "Terms of Service", path: "/terms-of-service" },
  ]),
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Service"
  description="Terms governing use of the Website Support Studio website, checkout, accounts, customer portal, and managed website support services."
  path="/terms-of-service"
  schemas={schemas}
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="prose">
      <nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="/">home</a><span class="sep">/</span><span><Label text="terms_of_service" /></span>
      </nav>
      <p class="kicker"><Label text="_legal" /></p>
      <h1><Label text="terms_of_service" /></h1>
      <p style="color:var(--text-muted);">Effective {LEGAL_EFFECTIVE_DATE}</p>

      <div class="summary" style="margin:1.5rem 0;">
        <strong>Summary.</strong> These terms govern use of Website Support Studio's public site, checkout,
        account access, customer portal, and managed website services. Paid engagements may also be governed
        by an order form, statement of work, or written agreement.
      </div>

      <h2>1. Agreement to these terms</h2>
      <p>
        By using Website Support Studio (the "Service"), you agree to these Terms. If you use the Service
        for an organization, you represent that you have authority to bind that organization.
      </p>

      <h2>2. Who provides the service</h2>
      <p>
        The Service is operated by {ORG.legalName}, organized in the {ORG.jurisdiction}, with its principal
        place of business in {ORG.address.locality}, {ORG.address.region}.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Website and service usage</h2>
      <p>
        You may use the public website to learn about WSS, view pricing, contact us, book a call, or start
        checkout. You may use the app only through an authorized account. You must not interfere with,
        reverse engineer, scrape, overload, or misuse the website, app, checkout flow, or support workflow.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Accounts and customer responsibilities</h2>
      <p>You are responsible for:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>using the same email or authorized account needed to connect checkout, onboarding, and workspace access;</li>
        <li>keeping account access secure and telling us promptly about suspected unauthorized use;</li>
        <li>providing accurate company, website, contact, platform, and request information;</li>
        <li>having the rights to any content, files, screenshots, credentials, domains, or website materials you provide;</li>
        <li>reviewing and approving work before launch or publication when approval is required;</li>
        <li>not submitting unlawful, infringing, malicious, confidential, or sensitive information unless it is necessary and you are authorized to share it.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>5. Customer portal and request workflow</h2>
      <p>
        The portal supports onboarding, website project visibility, website requests, attachments, status
        updates, and customer/operator workflow records. WSS may triage, draft, prepare, deliver, or close
        work based on the request details and the applicable plan or agreement. Some features may be staged,
        feature-gated, or unavailable in a given environment.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Payments</h2>
      <p>
        Payments and subscriptions are processed by Stripe. WSS may receive payment identifiers,
        subscription status, buyer email, customer identifiers, and related webhook data from Stripe to
        provision and manage your account. Fees, included work, renewal terms, cancellation terms, and
        refund terms are governed by the checkout flow and any applicable written agreement.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Intellectual property</h2>
      <p>
        WSS owns the Website Support Studio name, brand, public website, app interface, workflow system,
        documentation, software, and templates except for content owned by others. You retain ownership of
        materials you provide. You grant WSS the rights needed to use those materials to perform the
        Service. For website builds, ownership of final website deliverables is governed by the purchased
        package or written agreement.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Third-party services</h2>
      <p>
        The Service uses third-party providers including Vercel, Supabase, Stripe, Google services, and
        email/notification providers. Your use of third-party services, including Stripe Checkout, Google
        OAuth, Google Calendar, and LinkedIn, may be governed by their own terms and policies.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Service changes and availability</h2>
      <p>
        We may update, change, suspend, or discontinue parts of the website, app, checkout flow, or service
        features. We try to operate the Service reliably, but we do not guarantee uninterrupted or error-free
        operation.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Disclaimers</h2>
      <p>
        Except as expressly stated in a signed agreement, the Service and website are provided "as is" and
        "as available" without warranties of any kind, express or implied, including implied warranties of
        merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, title, and non-infringement. Website, SEO,
        analytics, lead, and business outcomes can vary and are not guaranteed unless expressly agreed in
        writing.
      </p>

      <h2>11. Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the maximum extent permitted by law, {ORG.legalName} and its owners, personnel, contractors, and
        providers will not be liable for indirect, incidental, special, consequential, exemplary, or punitive
        damages, or for lost profits, lost revenue, lost data, loss of goodwill, or business interruption.
        To the maximum extent permitted by law, total liability arising from the Service will not exceed the
        greater of the amount you paid WSS for the Service in the three months before the event giving rise
        to the claim or US$100. Some jurisdictions do not allow certain limits, so some limits may not apply.
      </p>

      <h2>12. Suspension or termination</h2>
      <p>
        We may suspend or terminate access if you breach these Terms, fail to pay amounts due, misuse the
        Service, create security risk, or if suspension is needed to protect WSS, customers, providers, or
        the public. Terms that by their nature should survive will survive termination.
      </p>

      <h2>13. Governing law</h2>
      <p>
        These Terms are governed by the laws of the {ORG.jurisdiction}, without regard to conflict-of-law
        rules. Courts located in Florida will have exclusive jurisdiction unless a signed agreement says
        otherwise.
      </p>

      <h2>14. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about these Terms can be sent to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT.email}`}>{CONTACT.email}</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

